# Configuration 11 -- the v3 headline: three regions on a rail line.
#
#   [ Mine ] ==OreTrain, 1400 each way==> [ Smelting ] ==PlateTrain, 900==> [ Works ]
#
# Nothing here is new physics. What is new is that the three regions are
# *executed separately*, each with its own clock, exchanging nothing but
# timestamped batches and timestamped empty vehicles.
#
# The trains declare a distance rather than a latency. That matters more than
# it looks: a distance is symmetric, so the vehicle takes as long to come back
# as it took to go, and it is the trip home that gives the *sending* region its
# licence to run ahead. A v2 link teleported home, which is a zero-latency
# channel running backwards through the transport, and it pins the loading end
# to the unloading end forever.
#
# Rates, so the plant has real tension in it rather than a comfortable margin:
#
#   miners        6 x 300 / 60           = 30.00 ore  /tick
#   ore train     8 x 6000 / 2800        = 17.14 ore  /tick   <- bottleneck
#   smelters     40 x 25 / 50            = 20.00 ore  /tick of appetite
#   plate train  10 x 3000 / 1800        = 16.67 plate/tick
#   gear presses 60 x 20 / 60            = 20.00 plate/tick of appetite
#   depots        4 x 150 / 60           = 10.00 gear /tick of appetite
#
# So the mine head fills and the miners take backpressure, both trains run
# saturated, and both downstream regions run hungry. Every region therefore has
# something to do at almost every tick, which is the case where an
# independently-advancing scheduler has the least to gain -- deliberately, so
# the measured speed-up is not an artifact of a plant that is mostly asleep.

item IronOre
item IronPlate
item Gear

blueprint RailChain {
    source  Miner x6     { produces 300 IronOre every 60 ticks }
    storage MineHead     { capacity 120000  policy round_robin }

    link    OreTrain x8  {
        moves 6000 IronOre
        distance 2400 speed 2 base 200      # 200 + 1200 = 1400 ticks each way
    }

    storage Yard         { capacity 120000  policy round_robin }
    process Smelter x40  { consumes 25 IronOre takes 50 ticks produces 25 IronPlate }
    storage PlateBay     { capacity 80000   policy round_robin }

    link    PlateTrain x10 {
        moves 3000 IronPlate
        takes 900 ticks
        returns 900 ticks
    }

    storage Works        { capacity 80000   policy round_robin }
    process GearPress x60 { consumes 20 IronPlate takes 60 ticks produces 10 Gear }
    storage GearBay      { capacity 40000   policy round_robin }
    sink    Depot x4     { consumes 150 Gear every 60 ticks }

    wire Miner -> MineHead -> OreTrain -> Yard -> Smelter -> PlateBay
    wire PlateBay -> PlateTrain -> Works -> GearPress -> GearBay -> Depot
}

deploy 1 x RailChain
